1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,919
In the Numismatists Discord,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:03,160
DOPEMIND asked:

3
00:00:03,359 --> 00:00:05,759
"What should I add to expand the set?

4
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:08,487
Wondering about the direction for this collection."

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,279
As of November 2026, DOPEMIND's Wall

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:16,646
on cents.vision holds 12 Cents, from 1963 to 1981.

7
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:19,839
centoshi replied: "You already know my answer."

8
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,567
DOPEMIND wrote back: "1971."

9
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,960
centoshi holds 16 Cents from 1971,

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,847
more than any other collector.

11
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:30,507
Of 1971, Martin Lehnen wrote:

12
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,560
"It was the year the United States abandoned

13
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,719
the gold standard, severing the connection

14
00:00:34,799 --> 00:00:37,207
between currency and tangible value."

15
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:41,520
On November 9, 2026, three of the 362

16
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:44,406
Cents from 1971 were listed for sale.

17
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:47,600
Number 2779 is a Ghost Cent with full

18
00:00:47,679 --> 00:00:50,240
desert patina: pale toning that dominates

19
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:52,920
the coin and separates Lincoln from the field.

20
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:55,046
Only 13 Cents are both.

21
00:00:55,119 --> 00:00:58,612
Number 8556, a 1971 from Denver,

22
00:00:58,667 --> 00:01:00,399
is contaminated, with significant

23
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:03,127
verdigris: a major presence on the face.

24
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,840
And number 5298 carries no visual

25
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,167
trait: a clean record of its year.

26
00:01:08,239 --> 00:01:10,400
Any one of them would add the 1971

27
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,245
Club badge to DOPEMIND's Wall.

28
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:14,200
Daidatep suggested six more,

29
00:01:14,239 --> 00:01:17,719
and added: "I could go on and on." On the same day,

30
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:20,007
all six were listed for sale as well.

31
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:23,480
Number 8657 is from 1965.

32
00:01:23,519 --> 00:01:26,132
Only 90 Cents are from 1965,

33
00:01:26,186 --> 00:01:28,719
fewer than any other year of the 1960s,

34
00:01:28,799 --> 00:01:30,566
and none of them carries a mint mark.

35
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,599
It has a notable desert patina:

36
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:34,498
clearly visible, but local.

37
00:01:34,701 --> 00:01:37,079
Number 8820, from 1972,

38
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,599
carries two patinas:

39
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,893
verdigris along the rim,

40
00:01:39,947 --> 00:01:42,200
and significant red across the face.

41
00:01:42,239 --> 00:01:45,206
183 Cents have significant red.

42
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,879
On DOPEMIND's Wall, it would complete

43
00:01:46,959 --> 00:01:50,007
a Patina Set: all four base patinas.

44
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:54,439
Number 6451, from 1980, has significant obsidian:

45
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:57,239
dark toning that pushes the copper into shadow.

46
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,239
220 Cents have it.

47
00:01:59,352 --> 00:02:03,000
Number 6875, from 1967,

48
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:06,319
is one of 44 heavily abraded Cents.

49
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:07,519
In the Traits Atlas,

50
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,800
heavy abrasion "dominates the read of the coin."

51
00:02:10,879 --> 00:02:14,879
Number 6782 is a 1969 from Denver,

52
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:17,520
with obsidian and significant verdigris.

53
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,919
It would add the 1969 Club badge.

54
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,680
And number 5888 is a 1956 from Denver,

55
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,360
with notable verdigris.

56
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,840
Only 28 Cents are from 1956, 18 of them from Denver.

57
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:31,706
It would be the Wall's first wheat penny.

58
00:02:32,217 --> 00:02:33,360
To see every Cent listed

59
00:02:33,439 --> 00:02:35,439
for sale, switch cents.vision

60
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,800
from Lab to Market.

61
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:38,879
What should DOPEMIND add next?

62
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,000
Tell us what you think.
